  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Dribble over the line",
  "description": "A 3v3 game without goals. Each team defends one end line and attacks the other. You score by dribbling the ball over the opponents' line and stopping it with your foot – not by shooting.\n\nIt works just as well 2v2 or 4v4. Make the pitch wider if it gets crowded. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep the ball close when you dribble, and use your laces when there is free space ahead."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up – is it open ahead, or should you pass to a teammate?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defenders: stand between the ball and your line."
    }
  ],
